{"availability":"available","full":"fancy-regex/fancy-regex","name":"fancy-regex","description":"Rust library for regular expressions using \"fancy\" features like look-around and backreferences. Has a mode which aims to be compatible with Oniguruma syntax.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":636,"forks":55,"created":"2018-10-02T17:55:03Z","updated":"2026-10-13T18:04:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fancy-regex.github.io/fancy-regex/","topics":["regex","regular-expressions"],"demo":"https://fancy-regex.github.io/fancy-regex/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:19.589Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:19.589Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T16:01:19.589Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:36.109Z","stars":634,"forks":55},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:13.981Z","stars":634,"forks":55},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:10.183Z","stars":634,"forks":55},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:25.071Z","stars":635,"forks":55},{"at":"2026-10-11T09:01:26.515Z","stars":635,"forks":55},{"at":"2026-10-17T16:01:19.589Z","stars":636,"forks":55}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Rust library for compiling and matching regular expressions. It uses a hybrid regex implementation designed to support a relatively rich set of features. In particular, it uses backtracking to implement \"fancy\" features such as look-around and backtracking, which are not supported in purely NFA-based implementations (exemplified by RE2, and implemented in Rust in the regex crate).","Try it online in the fancy-regex playground - test and explore regular expressions with advanced features in your browser.","A goal is to be as efficient as possible. For a given regex, the NFA implementation has asymptotic running time linear in the length of the input, while in the general case a backtracking implementation has exponential blowup. An example given in Static Analysis for Regular Expression Exponential Runtime via S